# Questing Druid: "Whenever you cast a spell that's white, blue, black, or red, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature." Boros Charm
# is red and white, and still triggers it only once (the ruling: one counter, not two). Mox Ruby and Mox Pearl (colorless artifact
# spells), Ornithopter (colorless) and Llanowar Elves (green) cast while the Druid is on the battlefield trigger nothing; neither does
# the Druid's own casting (it is not on the battlefield yet). Everything happens in turn 1 but the Elves, cast in turn 3.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Questing Druid
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Boros Charm
Ornithopter
Llanowar Elves
Forest x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Questing Druid.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Questing Druid.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Boros Charm.Cast
Bot1.Modes(1)
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
[T1 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Questing Druid.Power = 2
? Bot1.Battlefield.Questing Druid.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 16
Bot1.Battlefield.Questing Druid.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Questing Druid.Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Questing Druid.Toughness = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Tapped = false
